\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n--------------------------------\nStep 3.5-1 Competitive Response:\nJ&J submitted Ottava to FDA in Jan 2026 and reportedly received De Novo authorization July 22, 2026 [Estimate \u2014 secondary source The Bot Scout]. Medtronic Hugo performed first US commercial cases in early 2026 [Estimate \u2014 MedTech Dive]. Counter-move impact: \u22122 (price pressure on systems, slower placement growth, hospital procurement optionality).\nStep 3.5-2 Reflexivity:\nPositive loop: installed-base growth \u2192 data \u2192 better outcomes \u2192 more training \u2192 network effects. Negative loop: the 38% stock decline [Arithmetic 603.88\u2192374.91] reduces SBC recruiting currency; but ISRG's cash position and margins insulate it.\nStep 3.5-3 Customer Behavior:\nEarly adopters (large academic centers) already saturated; mainstream hospitals increasingly price-sensitive. LTV/CAC stable but attach rates for Ion/SP remain unproven at scale. Churn near zero for installed base.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n--------------------------------\nPrior (from 1.5): P(outperform over 5 yrs) = 45%.\nUpdate triggers: Q2 2026 beat (+$0.29 vs consensus [Actual]), maintained FY guidance [Actual], Ottava De Novo [Estimate], FDA stapler safety communication [Estimate]. Posterior P(base/bull) = 55% [Assumption].\nScenario probabilities (total = 100%):\n- Bear (25%): Competition + FDA + hospital budget freeze. Revenue CAGR 8% to 2030, OM 28% terminal. IV = $150.\n- Base (50%): Procedure growth decelerates from 16% to 5\u20137% by 2031, OM 33.5%. IV = $206