-3 Core Anchored Stack:\nEV = 2.52 \u00d7 3.5 + 7.55 \u00d7 4.5 (= EV/GP benchmark) + 2.52 \u00d7 25 + 7.55 \u00d7 5.5 (hybrid blend) \u2248 8.8 + 34.0 + 63.0 + 41.5 = 147.3B, pre-net-cash. Post-net-cash equity = 156.3B \u21d2 $436/share [Estimate]. This is the \"platform multiple\" result \u2014 it embeds the market's forward optimism. It will be discarded as the primary anchor because it assumes the platform multiple persists indefinitely.\n\nStep 3-4 Primary: UFCF DCF (9-year explicit, TV 3.0%):\nForecast drivers \u2014 revenue growth (labeled [Assumption] unless tagged):\n- FY2026: 12.55B (+14.0% vs FY25; guided procedure growth 13.5\u201315.5% [Actual company], pricing ~flat)\n- FY2027: 14.18B (+13.0%) [Assumption \u2014 decelerating from competition]\n- FY2028: 15.81B (+11.5%) [Assumption]\n- FY2029: 17.39B (+10.0%) [Assumption]\n- FY2030: 18.96B (+9.0%) [Assumption]\n- FY2031: 20.47B (+8.0%) [Assumption]\n- FY2032: 21.91B (+7.0%) [Assumption]\n- FY2033: 23.22B (+6.0%) [Assumption]\n- FY2034: 24.38B (+5.0%) [Assumption]\nPost-2034 terminal growth 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 capped at long-run nominal GDP].\nOperating margin path: 29.5% \u2192 33.5% by 2034 (operating leverage + mix shift to services; competition caps upside) [Assumption].\nTax rate: 18% [Assumption \u2014 derived from pack's \"tax identity holds\" note, but the exact consolidated rate is [Unconfirmed]; a 2pt change moves IV \u00b13%].\nD&A: 6.0% of revenue [Assumption \u2014 matches FY2025 0.613/10.065 = 6.1%].\nCapex: 6.0% of revenue [Assumption \u2014 FY2025 0.540/10.065 = 5.4%, TTM 0.484/11.034 = 4.4%; 6% builds in the construction cycle noted in the pack's 10-Q quote].\n\u0394WC: 2% of incremental revenue [Assumption \u2014 excludes cash/investment swings].\nDiscount-rate derivation:\n- Risk-free: 4.71% [Actual, TradingEconomics]\n- ERP: 4.50% [Assumption \u2014 long-run US equity premium]\n- Beta: 1.25 [Assumption \u2014 vendor reports 1.46 [Actual vendor] but the untagged window likely includes the 2025-26 drawdown; 1.25 reflects recurring-revenue stability. A 1.46 beta would raise WACC to ~11.3% and lower IV ~8%.]\n- Cost of equity: 4.71% + 1.25\u00d74.50% = 10.34% [Arithmetic]\n- Cost of debt: 5.2% pre-tax [Estimate; moot, no debt]\n- WACC: 10.3% [Assumption]\n\nUFCF table (B):\n| FY | Rev | OI | NOPAT | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | UFCF |\n| 2026 | 12.55 | 3.70 | 3.04 | 0.75 | 0.75 | 0.05 | 2.99 |\n| 2027 | 14.18 | 4.25 | 3.49 | 0.85 | 0.85 | 0.03 | 3.46 |\n| 2028 | 15.81 | 4.82 | 3.95 | 0.95 | 0.95 | 0.03 | 3.92 |\n| 2029 | 17.39 | 5.39 | 4.42 | 1.04 | 1.04 | 0.03 | 4.39 |\n| 2030 | 18.96 | 5.97 | 4.90 | 1.14 | 1.14 | 0.03 | 4.87 |\n| 2031 | 20.47 | 6.55 | 5.37 | 1.23 | 1.23 | 0.03 | 5.34 |\n| 2032 | 21.91 | 7.12 | 5.84 | 1.31 | 1.31 | 0.03 | 5.81 |\n| 2033 | 23.22 | 7.66 | 6.28 | 1.39 | 1.39 | 0.03 | 6.26 |\n| 2034 | 24.38 | 8.17 | 6.70 | 1.46 | 1.46 | 0.02 | 6.67 |\nPV of explicit UFCF at 10.3% = 25.9B [Arithmetic].\nTerminal value at 2034 = 6.67\u00d71.03/(0.103\u22120.03) = 94.2B [Arithmetic]. PV of TV = 39.0B [Arithmetic].\nEV = 25.9 + 39.0 = 64.9B.\nNet cash: +9.03B (cash 3.368 + ST investments 2.567 + LT investments 3.099) [Actual filing values; overlap risk flagged in pack, but ISRG's debt is zero, so double-count risk is low].\nEquity value = 73.9B. Per share = 73.9/0.3583 = $206 [Arithmetic].\nIV base (DCF) = $206. This is the disciplined anchor.\n\nStep 3-5 Tornado Sensitivity (top 3 variables):\n1. Revenue CAGR 2026\u201334 (10% vs 12%): IV $188\u2013$230 [\u00b110%].\n2. Terminal margin (31% vs 36%): IV $190\u2013$225 [\u00b18%].\n3. WACC (9.3% vs 11.3%): IV $185\u2013$235 [\u00b112%].\nConclusion: Even the most favorable combination ($235) is below T0 of $375.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25